#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Let Claude Code and Codex sessions on this host message each other by name.

Claude sessions already message each other natively (SendMessage,
/list-agents), and a Codex session takes a message from outside with `codex
queue`. This daemon joins the two:

  into Codex   `codex queue`, whoever sends;
  into Claude  one line written into the session's inbox socket - the socket
               Claude Code documents for scripts to post into - as SendMessage
               itself writes it. Its `from` is a reply socket kept here for the
               Codex session sending, so a SendMessage reply to that address
               comes back here and is queued into that session.

Agents send with `agent-bridge send` from their shell, which carries
CODEX_THREAD_ID or CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID. Codex sessions are not in Claude's
/list-agents: a Claude session starts a conversation with one by `agent-bridge
send` as well, and answers one with SendMessage to the uds: address its message
came from. The daemon starts on demand (any subcommand but status and stop) and
keeps a reply socket for each live Codex session that has had a first message.

Design 1 put a headless Claude "stand-in" in front of each Codex session
instead. It is kept on the branch agent-bridge-design1;
plans/agent-bridge-claude-codex-messaging.md describes both designs.
"""
